From: accel-virt
Subject: [PATCH] d3d9 RESZ is a known driver hack format, not an unknown one

RESZ is the FOURCC applications probe through CheckDeviceFormat for the resolve-depth hack, which CheckDeviceFormat answers itself for render targets; every other probe and every surface description reached ConvertFormat's default case and logged an unknown format warning per call, so a probe loop filled the log. It is handled as unsupported without a warning, as the other driver hack FOURCCs are.
---
diff -ruN
--- a/src/d3d9/d3d9_format.cpp
+++ b/src/d3d9/d3d9_format.cpp
@@ -397,6 +397,8 @@
 
       case D3D9Format::SSAA: return {}; // Driver hack, handled elsewhere
 
+      case D3D9Format::RESZ: return {}; // Driver hack, handled elsewhere
+
       case D3D9Format::INTZ: return {
         VK_FORMAT_D24_UNORM_S8_UINT,
         VK_FORMAT_UNDEFINED,
